+/-! A function item used as a closure (`iter.map(f)`, with the instance `BuiltinFnMut`) is the
+state of the adapter (`Map { iter, f }`), and the consumers of the adapter give their final
+state back, so a recursive function passed that way would be a value in the flat order of
+`Result`, where it is not monotone. The consumers below are the same as the consumers of a
+stateless closure which calls the function, whose instance (not state) depends on it; the
+`aeneas_monotonicity` tactic rewrites them so, and `aeneas_fix_monotone` shows the fixpoints of
+the consumers (`iterToList`, `foldFromNext`) monotone in the instance. The equations are proved
+by fixpoint induction from maps of the states which commute with the steps of the fixpoints. -/
